WEBVTT

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:38.932
We shouldn't be here.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:39.972
Don't worry.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.201
Nobody saw us leave.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:45.733
Hey, I need that.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.780
What if somebody tries to call?

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.075
Shh.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.643
What was that?

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.983
Don't worry.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.419
Come here.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.839
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:03.109
After two weeks, we're close

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.878
to repairing
the Varro's warp drive.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.179
Then there's the Varro crew.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.276
I'm starting to think

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.184
they'd rather give up
warp travel than accept

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:10.882
help from strangers.

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.117
I thought we agreed

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:14.023
Central Control
would be off-limits.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:16.721
We did, but I need to access
your warp assembly.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.161
That technology's classified.

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:19.528
We have to reconfigure
the assembly

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:20.861
if we're going
to finish this job.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:21.923
Then consider it finished.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.298
We've come this far...

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.462
You've turned our ship
upside down for two weeks.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.369
I've yet to see any results.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.670
You might check
the antimatter injectors.

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:34.643
Back on line.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.807
All you need now is
a jolt of antimatter

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.545
from Voyager's engines
and you'll be back in business,

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.782
but I need access
to your warp assembly.

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:45.519
You know, I can understand

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:47.617
why you're distrustful
of other species.

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:50.925
Frankly, we've had a rough time
in the Delta Quadrant ourselves,

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:53.522
but our two species have
made remarkable progress,

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.625
working together
to repair your engines.

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:56.862
We've come a long way

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.961
since you ignored
our opening hails.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.766
Let's not throw all that away.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.799
I'll admit we do share
some things in common.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:07.744
We're both on long journeys,
looking for allies.

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:10.248
In many ways,
we're like cousins.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.305
"Cousins"?

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:13.249
Well, distant cousins...
think about it.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:16.186
400 years ago, you started
out the same way we did...

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:20.716
a single starship, a small crew,
facing the unknown

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.454
and now, centuries later,

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.689
you've grown
into a generational ship

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.925
with a history
and culture all your own.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.525
When I look at your vessel,
I can't help but wonder

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.763
if I'm seeing Voyager's future.

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:34.932
Our journey could easily last
several generations.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.804
So, what do you say...
cousin?

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:41.443
You can access the warp
assembly from here.

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:42.913
Thank you.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:43.914
Status?

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.314
Their plasma couplings
are on line.

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:46.943
We're ready
for the antimatter transfer.

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:48.781
Then let's get started.

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:49.947
Janeway to Voyager.
Status?

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.249
Ready here, Captain.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.985
Initiate the transfer.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:59.259
Warp reactors 1 through 14
are coming on line.

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:00.264
It's working.

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.823
Keep your fingers crossed.

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.231
For luck.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.856
If you're planning on leaving

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:28.917
through the viewport,
you might want to get dressed.

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:32.487
The interstellar vacuum
might get a little chilly.

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:34.555
What?

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:38.502
Oh. Funny.

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:40.505
Come back to bed.

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:41.904
I can't sleep.

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.066
Cuddle.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.575
I can't cuddle.

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:47.112
I told you we're not
going to get caught.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.546
If someone had seen us, they
would've reported it by now.

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:51.947
I'm violating
about half a dozen regulations

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:54.952
by just being in this room,
and what we did earlier...

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:58.046
I don't know if Starfleet
even has a regulation for that.

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.455
What are you saying?

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:02.119
Making love is a crime
in your culture?

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:07.633
Yes! No. What I'm saying is
it's a breach of protocol.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.895
How romantic.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:12.027
The Captain instructed
all away teams...

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:14.300
no personal interaction
with the Varro crew.

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:15.739
I violated a direct order.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:17.503
Come back to bed.

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:19.067
That's an order.

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:27.181
Are all humans so jumpy?

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.220
No.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:29.754
Only me.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:35.092
The warp engines.

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:38.426
They started
the plasma transfer.

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:40.489
We've got to get down there.

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:41.555
We're late.

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.564
What are you waiting for?

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:46.434
To see what you look like
in my uniform.

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:51.775
You don't understand.

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:53.505
If I'm not at my post...

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:54.773
You'll be executed.

00:06:54.847 --> 00:06:56.212
Funny.

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:58.113
We better go in separately.

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:08.653
Impressive.

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:11.595
Just trying to orchestrate
the antimatter flow.

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:14.064
You should try some Chopin
when you're done.

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:16.567
Look who showed up
for the final movement.

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:17.568
Excuse me?

00:07:17.637 --> 00:07:19.605
Just a little late for the joke

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:21.264
as well as the job.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:24.275
I was checking the manifolds
in Segment 22.

00:07:28.114 --> 00:07:30.014
Warp reaction's destabilizing.

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:31.379
Tal?

00:07:32.685 --> 00:07:33.947
I can't find the problem.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:40.486
We're less than a minute away
from multiple core breaches.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.255
Abort the transfer.

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:46.827
So much for finger crossing.

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:48.264
B'Elanna.

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:50.461
I'm reading microfractures
all over the hull.

00:07:50.536 --> 00:07:52.128
Why couldn't we detect
that before?

00:07:52.205 --> 00:07:53.137
Good question.

00:07:53.206 --> 00:07:54.138
We'll have to check the hulls

00:07:54.207 --> 00:07:55.299
on each
of your vessel's segments.

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:56.306
But that'll take days.

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:58.070
The sooner we start,
the sooner we finish.

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:06.552
Friendly people.

00:08:06.619 --> 00:08:08.519
They've had a lot
of bad experiences

00:08:08.588 --> 00:08:09.612
with other species.

00:08:09.689 --> 00:08:10.883
Well, I don't know.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:13.823
It seems like your first
contact went pretty well.

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:15.360
What's that supposed to mean?

00:08:15.428 --> 00:08:17.862
I'm just wondering where
you disappeared to today.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:18.897
I told you.

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:20.659
I was checking
the plasma conduits in...

00:08:20.733 --> 00:08:22.701
In Segment 22.
I know.

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:24.895
They must have sonic
showers over there.

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:27.835
You're a lot cleaner than
you were when you left.

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:31.070
You are such a lousy liar.

00:08:31.143 --> 00:08:32.405
Haven't you learned
anything from me

00:08:32.478 --> 00:08:33.410
after five years?

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:34.446
She's cute.

00:08:34.514 --> 00:08:35.446
Who?

00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:37.574
That assistant engineer, Tal.

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:39.584
Cute enough.

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:42.416
Oh, here we go again.

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:43.420
What?!

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:46.014
You. Going after
impossible women...

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:50.290
a hologram, an ex-Borg,
the wrong twin,

00:08:50.363 --> 00:08:52.831
and now a girl
from a xenophobic species?

00:08:52.899 --> 00:08:55.299
You're right.
You're absolutely right.

00:08:55.368 --> 00:08:56.926
I'm putting her out of my mind.
I promise.

00:08:57.036 --> 00:08:58.765
Good. Glad to hear it.

00:08:58.838 --> 00:09:00.601
I'm due back on the Bridge.

00:09:00.673 --> 00:09:02.038
See you in the morning.

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:07.841
Computer, open a channel
to Varro ship,

00:09:07.914 --> 00:09:09.643
Segment 16, Station 204.

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:12.878
Encode transmission with
security protocol Alpha-7.

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:14.077
Channel open.

00:09:14.153 --> 00:09:15.620
What took you so long?

00:09:15.688 --> 00:09:18.020
I've been waiting 22 minutes
for you to call.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.887
I was testing myself,

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:22.688
seeing how long
I could resist calling you.

00:09:22.762 --> 00:09:23.820
And?

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:27.059
I lasted 22 minutes.

00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:29.533
Should I feel complimented
or insulted?

00:09:29.602 --> 00:09:34.096
Since this is the first chance
I've had to open a com-link...

00:09:34.173 --> 00:09:35.299
complimented.

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:39.868
So... you liked what happened.

00:09:39.946 --> 00:09:42.915
Yeah. A lot.

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:44.915
Enough to try it again?

00:09:45.017 --> 00:09:48.350
Absolutely,
but I've got to be honest.

00:09:48.421 --> 00:09:52.357
I wasn't expecting something
so... different.

00:09:52.425 --> 00:09:54.290
Neither was I.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.453
Our species look so similar.

00:09:56.529 --> 00:09:57.928
Well, at least on the surface.

00:09:57.997 --> 00:09:59.294
I would've never guessed

00:09:59.365 --> 00:10:01.060
when it came down
to the basics...

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:02.327
well, let's just say,

00:10:02.401 --> 00:10:04.426
the birds and bees
would be very confused.

00:10:04.503 --> 00:10:07.301
"Birds and bees"?

00:10:07.373 --> 00:10:08.431
I'm telling you,

00:10:08.507 --> 00:10:10.202
you should take a look
at their database.

00:10:10.276 --> 00:10:13.177
They've got some pretty
amazing stuff on that ship.

00:10:13.245 --> 00:10:14.712
Stuff.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.715
Well, their environmental
control systems, for instance...

00:10:17.783 --> 00:10:19.614
it's completely regenerative.

00:10:19.685 --> 00:10:21.118
Zero waste.

00:10:21.187 --> 00:10:22.381
Impressive.

00:10:22.455 --> 00:10:25.447
It can be programmed to create
almost any habitat.

00:10:25.524 --> 00:10:27.719
If you wanted to,
you could recreate Vulcan

00:10:27.793 --> 00:10:29.351
in your quarters
with that system.

00:10:29.428 --> 00:10:30.895
Why would I want to?

00:10:30.963 --> 00:10:33.488
A little taste of home
in the Delta Quadrant?

00:10:33.566 --> 00:10:34.965
Think about it...

00:10:35.101 --> 00:10:38.093
springtime on the shores
of Lake Yuron.

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:40.968
I require a desk and a bed,
nothing more.

00:10:41.107 --> 00:10:42.836
You're missing the point.

00:10:42.908 --> 00:10:43.966
No doubt.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:47.511
These people have been
traveling for 400 years.

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:50.140
They've learned a thing or two
about living comfortably.

00:10:50.216 --> 00:10:52.207
Our systems
are more than adequate.

00:10:53.285 --> 00:10:54.252
I give up.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.584
After only two minutes?

00:10:56.656 --> 00:10:58.180
Tuvok, how do you do it?

00:10:58.257 --> 00:11:01.090
I wait until his own
illogic overwhelms him.

00:11:03.562 --> 00:11:05.860
I'm detecting
an unauthorized transmission.

00:11:05.931 --> 00:11:06.898
Origin?

00:11:06.966 --> 00:11:07.898
Unknown.

00:11:07.967 --> 00:11:09.264
It's been encoded.

00:11:09.335 --> 00:11:11.496
Find out where it's going.

00:11:13.806 --> 00:11:17.105
Where would you
most like to be right now?

00:11:17.176 --> 00:11:18.905
Besides your quarters?

00:11:18.978 --> 00:11:20.468
Besides my quarters.

00:11:20.546 --> 00:11:22.343
On a distant moon,

00:11:22.415 --> 00:11:25.248
where the air is warm
and the gravity is light.

00:11:25.317 --> 00:11:27.114
No bulkheads around me.

00:11:27.186 --> 00:11:30.587
Where, if I walk too quickly,
I can almost fly.

00:11:30.656 --> 00:11:32.351
I like that.

00:11:32.425 --> 00:11:34.086
What about you?

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:37.527
Where would you most want
to be right now?

00:11:37.596 --> 00:11:38.756
Besides your cabin?

00:11:39.932 --> 00:11:41.490
Besides my cabin.

00:11:41.567 --> 00:11:42.693
Sorry. I can't come up

00:11:42.768 --> 00:11:44.633
with anything better
than your cabin.

00:11:44.704 --> 00:11:48.470
And what would you do
if you were here?

00:11:48.541 --> 00:11:49.633
Now?

00:11:49.709 --> 00:11:52.371
This very moment.

00:11:52.445 --> 00:11:55.972
I'd ask you to dim the lights.

00:11:56.115 --> 00:12:00.518
And what if I said... no?

00:12:00.586 --> 00:12:04.113
Okay. So, we leave
the lights on.

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:06.920
The message has been sent
to the Varro ship.

00:12:07.059 --> 00:12:07.923
Segment 16.

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:09.152
Living quarters.

00:12:10.663 --> 00:12:12.028
Uh, Commander?

00:12:12.098 --> 00:12:16.091
I think I can track
that down for you.

00:12:16.168 --> 00:12:18.830
Hold on.
Something's wrong.

00:12:18.904 --> 00:12:20.428
I'm losing the signal.

00:12:22.308 --> 00:12:23.570
Tal?

00:12:23.642 --> 00:12:25.542
The transmission has ended.

00:12:25.611 --> 00:12:26.908
If it was a transmission.

00:12:26.979 --> 00:12:29.573
Could have just been
a glitch in the com system.

00:12:29.648 --> 00:12:30.910
Run a diagnostic.

00:12:35.054 --> 00:12:36.681
Finding the source
of these structural problems

00:12:36.756 --> 00:12:37.882
isn't going to be easy.

00:12:37.957 --> 00:12:39.424
They've already scanned
most of their ship

00:12:39.492 --> 00:12:40.686
and come up empty.

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.352
I'm hoping
we'll do a better job.

00:12:42.428 --> 00:12:45.192
We should form smaller teams
to maximize efficiency.

00:12:45.264 --> 00:12:47.198
Agreed.
We'll work in pairs.

00:12:47.266 --> 00:12:50.099
Now, what I'd like to do is
start with their reactor room

00:12:50.169 --> 00:12:51.796
where we first
detected the problem...

00:12:51.871 --> 00:12:53.532
You owe me.

00:12:53.606 --> 00:12:54.538
What?

00:12:54.607 --> 00:12:55.767
Eyes front.

00:12:55.841 --> 00:12:58.401
Last night I had to
sabotage the com system

00:12:58.477 --> 00:13:00.274
to cover your tracks.

00:13:00.346 --> 00:13:01.643
You called her, didn't you?

00:13:01.714 --> 00:13:03.147
Guilty.

00:13:03.215 --> 00:13:05.046
How long has this been going on?

00:13:05.117 --> 00:13:06.607
The truth.

00:13:06.685 --> 00:13:08.880
From the moment
we first saw each other.

00:13:08.954 --> 00:13:11.548
It was like touching
an open plasma relay.

00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:13.922
Hmm. Sounds serious.

00:13:13.993 --> 00:13:15.551
Maybe it is.

00:13:15.628 --> 00:13:16.686
Has it occurred to you

00:13:16.762 --> 00:13:18.923
that you're breaking
a few dozen protocols?

00:13:18.998 --> 00:13:21.398
We know what we're getting into.

00:13:22.601 --> 00:13:23.693
Do you?

00:13:23.769 --> 00:13:24.793
Our duty assignment.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:25.802
We're to survey

00:13:25.871 --> 00:13:27.634
the generational ship
from Astrometrics.

00:13:32.378 --> 00:13:34.846
Teams Alpha and Gamma
have finished scanning

00:13:34.914 --> 00:13:36.279
Sections 1 through 64.

00:13:36.348 --> 00:13:39.146
Kind of puts a Borg cube
to shame, doesn't it?

00:13:39.218 --> 00:13:41.550
The vessel's technology
is impressive,

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.747
but its construction
is haphazard.

00:13:43.823 --> 00:13:46.553
I guess they sort of improvised
as they went along.

00:13:48.828 --> 00:13:52.559
Seven, you've been around
humans for a while now.

00:13:52.631 --> 00:13:55.964
What do you think about love?

00:13:56.035 --> 00:13:58.526
We're scanning
for microfractures.

00:13:58.604 --> 00:14:00.469
I don't see the relevance.

00:14:00.539 --> 00:14:03.133
Just curious.

00:14:03.209 --> 00:14:05.905
Parental love, romantic love,

00:14:06.045 --> 00:14:08.411
affection between friends.
Specify.

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:10.607
Romantic love.

00:14:10.683 --> 00:14:13.311
An attraction based
on sexual desire,

00:14:13.385 --> 00:14:15.751
one that facilitates
procreation.

00:14:15.821 --> 00:14:17.686
I guess I'm asking
the wrong person.

00:14:17.756 --> 00:14:19.417
Not at all.
The Borg have referenced

00:14:19.491 --> 00:14:22.392
this condition in over 6,000
assimilated species.

00:14:22.461 --> 00:14:26.022
"Condition"? You make it sound
like a disease.

00:14:26.098 --> 00:14:27.861
Physiologically, it bears

00:14:27.933 --> 00:14:29.798
a striking similarity
to disease.

00:14:29.869 --> 00:14:31.769
A series
of biochemical responses

00:14:31.837 --> 00:14:33.532
that trigger
an emotional cascade,

00:14:33.606 --> 00:14:35.699
impairing normal functioning.

00:14:35.774 --> 00:14:36.934
Forget it.

00:14:40.613 --> 00:14:43.275
Are you in love, Ensign?

00:14:47.753 --> 00:14:50.620
I guess that's what
I've been asking myself.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:57.456
You're glowing.

00:14:57.529 --> 00:14:59.292
I beg your pardon?

00:14:59.365 --> 00:15:01.959
Your epidermis luminesced.

00:15:02.034 --> 00:15:04.502
Huh...

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:06.037
Must be the lighting in here.

00:15:06.105 --> 00:15:08.335
No, it was you.

00:15:12.077 --> 00:15:13.169
You should report to Sick Bay.

00:15:13.245 --> 00:15:14.906
It's nothing.

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:16.607
You must comply.

00:15:20.986 --> 00:15:21.918
Lie still.

00:15:21.987 --> 00:15:22.919
I feel fine.

00:15:23.022 --> 00:15:24.455
No doubt
you're feeling wonderful.

00:15:24.523 --> 00:15:26.821
Your beta endorphins
are abnormally elevated.

00:15:26.892 --> 00:15:27.916
Really?

00:15:27.993 --> 00:15:28.925
You've been spending

00:15:28.994 --> 00:15:30.427
a lot of time
on the generational ship.

00:15:30.496 --> 00:15:32.930
Do you recall coming into
contact with any toxins?

00:15:32.998 --> 00:15:34.363
Antimatter radiation?

00:15:34.433 --> 00:15:35.764
No.

00:15:35.834 --> 00:15:37.563
Maybe something in one
of their medical bays...

00:15:37.636 --> 00:15:39.194
a biological agent?

00:15:39.271 --> 00:15:40.465
No.

00:15:40.539 --> 00:15:42.268
Did you consume
any of their cuisine?

00:15:42.341 --> 00:15:43.330
No.

00:15:43.409 --> 00:15:45.673
Doctor, there is unusual
synaptic activity

00:15:45.744 --> 00:15:47.302
in his cerebral cortex.

00:15:47.379 --> 00:15:48.812
No kidding.

00:15:48.881 --> 00:15:50.781
This could be the work
of an alien virus.

00:15:50.849 --> 00:15:52.714
We'll have to initiate
full quarantine protocols.

00:15:52.785 --> 00:15:55.151
Inform the Captain
and request a bio-alert.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:56.209
Wait.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:00.324
There's no need for that.

00:16:00.392 --> 00:16:01.359
I can explain.

00:16:01.427 --> 00:16:02.724
I'm listening.

00:16:06.298 --> 00:16:09.199
Could you give us some privacy?

00:16:09.268 --> 00:16:10.826
If there is the possibility
of an epidemic

00:16:10.903 --> 00:16:12.700
the Doctor may require
my assistance.

00:16:12.771 --> 00:16:15.899
There isn't and he won't.

00:16:15.975 --> 00:16:17.704
Please.

00:16:30.656 --> 00:16:34.422
Last night, I had an...

00:16:34.493 --> 00:16:36.620
encounter
with one of the Varro.

00:16:36.695 --> 00:16:38.424
Encounter?

00:16:38.497 --> 00:16:42.934
A... personal encounter.

00:16:43.002 --> 00:16:44.492
Specifically?

00:16:48.841 --> 00:16:51.401
Sex. We had sex.

00:16:51.477 --> 00:16:54.344
You had intimate contact
with an alien species

00:16:54.413 --> 00:16:55.471
without medical clearance?

00:16:55.547 --> 00:16:56.673
It was in the heat
of the moment.

00:16:56.749 --> 00:16:58.444
I didn't think anything
like this would happen.

00:16:58.517 --> 00:16:59.643
Correction.
If you'd been thinking,

00:16:59.718 --> 00:17:00.912
you would have
considered the risks

00:17:00.986 --> 00:17:02.783
and exercised restraint.

00:17:02.855 --> 00:17:04.049
Sit down.

00:17:04.123 --> 00:17:05.784
You'll need
a full biomedical workup,

00:17:05.858 --> 00:17:07.689
and your "friend"
will have to come in as well.

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:10.251
Do we have to drag her
into this?

00:17:10.329 --> 00:17:12.627
It is my medical responsibility,

00:17:12.698 --> 00:17:14.723
which, I'm sorry to say,
also requires me

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:16.267
to report this to the Captain.

00:17:25.644 --> 00:17:27.578
I expected more from you.

00:17:27.646 --> 00:17:29.841
I'm sorry.

00:17:29.915 --> 00:17:31.849
I... don't know
what I was thinking.

00:17:31.917 --> 00:17:33.350
Don't you?
I've seen Tal.

00:17:33.419 --> 00:17:35.910
She's an impressive young woman,
beautiful,

00:17:35.988 --> 00:17:37.216
but that's no excuse

00:17:37.289 --> 00:17:40.258
to ignore your obligations
as a Starfleet officer.

00:17:40.325 --> 00:17:41.383
Yes, ma'am.

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:43.325
There's a reason
you took a semester

00:17:43.395 --> 00:17:45.454
of interspecies protocol
at the Academy.

00:17:45.531 --> 00:17:46.930
There's also a reason

00:17:47.032 --> 00:17:49.057
why the Handbook
on Personal Relationships

00:17:49.134 --> 00:17:50.601
is three centimeters thick.

00:17:50.669 --> 00:17:52.034
"All Starfleet personnel must

00:17:52.104 --> 00:17:53.799
"obtain authorization
from their CO

00:17:53.872 --> 00:17:56.204
"as well as clearance
from their medical officer

00:17:56.275 --> 00:17:58.334
"before initiating
an intimate relationship

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:59.536
with an alien species."

00:17:59.611 --> 00:18:00.737
Bravo. Unfortunately,

00:18:00.813 --> 00:18:03.782
your recitation
comes a little late.

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:06.547
According to the Doctor,

00:18:06.618 --> 00:18:08.848
your condition isn't
life-threatening.

00:18:08.921 --> 00:18:11.890
There's no reason
to confine you to Sick Bay,

00:18:11.957 --> 00:18:14.448
but I do agree
with his recommendation

00:18:14.526 --> 00:18:17.689
to run full bio-scans
on both you and Tal.

00:18:19.598 --> 00:18:21.532
And her people need to be told,

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:24.125
so they can evaluate
any bio-threat

00:18:24.203 --> 00:18:27.468
you might've introduced
into their population.

00:18:27.539 --> 00:18:29.268
We're trying to help
these people, Ensign,

00:18:29.341 --> 00:18:30.899
earn their trust.

00:18:31.043 --> 00:18:32.032
I was even hoping

00:18:32.111 --> 00:18:34.909
they might return the favor,
share their technology,

00:18:35.013 --> 00:18:37.538
their insights into
long-term space travel,

00:18:37.616 --> 00:18:39.880
but your little escapade
put that in jeopardy.

00:18:40.953 --> 00:18:43.012
Permission to speak freely.

00:18:43.088 --> 00:18:45.283
With all due respect...

00:18:45.357 --> 00:18:48.053
this wasn't a fling.

00:18:48.127 --> 00:18:50.220
I've really gotten to know Tal,

00:18:50.295 --> 00:18:53.230
and I've developed
true feelings for her.

00:18:53.298 --> 00:18:54.697
Noted.

00:18:54.766 --> 00:18:58.031
But there are regulations,
and you've broken them.

00:18:58.103 --> 00:19:01.766
I'm entering a formal
reprimand into your record

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:03.398
and I'm ordering you
to break off

00:19:03.475 --> 00:19:04.737
this relationship.

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:06.107
Do you understand?

00:19:09.581 --> 00:19:10.707
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:10.782 --> 00:19:11.942
Dismissed.

00:19:20.659 --> 00:19:24.095
Commander, I wanted to share
a few security concerns.

00:19:24.163 --> 00:19:25.653
A few days ago, I noticed

00:19:25.731 --> 00:19:28.427
some Mess Hall supplies
had disappeared...

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:30.900
liquid nutriments,
emergency rations,

00:19:31.003 --> 00:19:33.301
nothing to warrant
a Red Alert, but...

00:19:33.372 --> 00:19:36.273
I took the liberty
of investigating on my own.

00:19:36.341 --> 00:19:38.275
Take a look at this.

00:19:38.343 --> 00:19:41.506
Unauthorized use
of the Mess Hall replicator

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:42.911
is hardly a felony.

00:19:43.015 --> 00:19:44.880
It wasn't just unauthorized.

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.713
Someone accessed the ship's

00:19:46.785 --> 00:19:49.618
environmental controls
from that station.

00:19:49.688 --> 00:19:53.886
Life support was routed
to Jefferies Tube G-33, Deck 15.

00:19:53.959 --> 00:19:56.928
Isn't that section
normally uninhabited?

00:19:57.029 --> 00:19:59.520
Whoever did this,
encoded the procedure

00:19:59.598 --> 00:20:01.327
so it wouldn't be detected.

00:20:16.381 --> 00:20:18.440
It appears we have intruders.

00:20:18.517 --> 00:20:21.315
It looks like
a Varro scanning device.

00:20:21.386 --> 00:20:24.719
Breathable oxygen is
confined to this chamber

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:27.953
and the area immediately
behind this hatch.

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:29.357
Stand back.

00:20:39.071 --> 00:20:40.368
Come in.

00:20:43.742 --> 00:20:45.334
Work?

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:48.345
No. I'm just tormenting myself
with what-ifs.

00:20:48.413 --> 00:20:49.744
What if I had the chance

00:20:49.815 --> 00:20:51.749
to actually see
that pulsar field,

00:20:51.817 --> 00:20:53.808
go there instead
of just squinting

00:20:53.885 --> 00:20:55.819
at it through
long-range sensors?

00:20:55.887 --> 00:20:57.616
Too far off your course, huh?

00:20:57.689 --> 00:20:59.589
Too close
to an inhabited planet.

00:20:59.658 --> 00:21:01.626
"They might make
contact with us."

00:21:01.693 --> 00:21:02.921
"It's too dangerous."

00:21:02.995 --> 00:21:04.622
It's always the same thing.

00:21:04.696 --> 00:21:06.891
The mighty generational ship.

00:21:06.965 --> 00:21:11.026
All we do is run away
from anything that's different.

00:21:12.104 --> 00:21:15.631
But that's going to change.

00:21:15.707 --> 00:21:18.005
I'm afraid
I've got some bad news.

00:21:24.716 --> 00:21:26.946
I, uh...

00:21:27.052 --> 00:21:29.043
I can't see you anymore.

00:21:29.121 --> 00:21:31.749
Captain's orders.

00:21:31.823 --> 00:21:34.053
How did she find out?

00:21:34.126 --> 00:21:36.219
Something happened
to me this morning.

00:21:36.295 --> 00:21:38.229
I had a strange sensation,

00:21:38.297 --> 00:21:40.231
and then my skin luminesced,
just like last night.

00:21:40.299 --> 00:21:42.893
That shouldn't have happened.

00:21:42.968 --> 00:21:45.766
Our species are too dissimilar.

00:21:45.837 --> 00:21:47.236
What shouldn't have happened?

00:21:48.307 --> 00:21:50.332
We call it olan'vora...

00:21:50.409 --> 00:21:51.967
"the shared heart."

00:21:52.044 --> 00:21:53.909
When two of us merge...

00:21:53.979 --> 00:21:56.812
You know
the biological connection

00:21:56.882 --> 00:21:58.406
we had last night?

00:21:58.483 --> 00:22:00.951
It becomes stronger.

00:22:01.019 --> 00:22:03.920
It won't hurt you, Harry,

00:22:04.022 --> 00:22:05.614
but it will change you.

00:22:05.691 --> 00:22:08.626
It'll change both of us...

00:22:08.694 --> 00:22:10.753
bring us closer.

00:22:10.829 --> 00:22:13.764
So, can this process
be reversed?

00:22:13.832 --> 00:22:15.993
In time...

00:22:18.036 --> 00:22:20.937
if we stay away from each other,

00:22:21.039 --> 00:22:23.303
but if we don't...

00:22:23.375 --> 00:22:25.104
the more we're together,

00:22:25.177 --> 00:22:27.668
the harder it will be
to stop it.

00:22:29.715 --> 00:22:32.309
But then, you have your orders.

00:22:32.384 --> 00:22:34.318
Orders.

00:22:36.722 --> 00:22:38.656
It's an old story.

00:22:38.724 --> 00:22:41.659
Boy meets girl from the
wrong side of the galaxy.

00:22:41.727 --> 00:22:42.955
Boy loses girl.

00:22:43.061 --> 00:22:45.529
And girl loses boy.

00:22:45.597 --> 00:22:49.328
It's not like we didn't know
this was going to end.

00:22:49.401 --> 00:22:52.837
At least we had two weeks.

00:22:52.904 --> 00:22:55.702
Two great weeks.

00:22:59.010 --> 00:23:00.307
Good-bye, Harry.

00:23:02.347 --> 00:23:03.644
Bye.

00:23:08.019 --> 00:23:11.284
Are you really going
to let me leave?

00:23:11.356 --> 00:23:14.917
If that's what you want.

00:23:15.026 --> 00:23:16.994
It's not.

00:23:19.364 --> 00:23:21.298
Welcome aboard.

00:23:21.366 --> 00:23:24.130
Normally we like to know
something about our guests

00:23:24.202 --> 00:23:25.931
before we invite them
to join us.

00:23:26.037 --> 00:23:27.937
Care to tell us
how you got here?

00:23:28.039 --> 00:23:29.370
Through a docking port.

00:23:29.441 --> 00:23:32.069
Your entry would have triggered
an intruder alert.

00:23:32.144 --> 00:23:35.113
Your technology
is easy to circumvent.

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:38.377
It doesn't matter
how I got here.

00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:41.044
I'm not going back.

00:23:41.119 --> 00:23:42.552
That remains to be seen.

00:23:42.621 --> 00:23:43.553
You haven't explained

00:23:43.622 --> 00:23:45.647
your reasons for leaving
the generational ship.

00:23:45.724 --> 00:23:48.284
I'm not a criminal,
if that's what you think.

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:50.726
If you leave me
at the next inhabited system,

00:23:50.796 --> 00:23:52.164
I'll manage from there.

00:23:52.230 --> 00:23:55.722
Your next stop is the brig
unless you answer my questions.

00:23:58.670 --> 00:24:01.070
I came aboard four days ago

00:24:01.139 --> 00:24:03.232
with one of the work details.

00:24:03.308 --> 00:24:04.104
Why?

00:24:05.177 --> 00:24:07.042
Our ship's not the paradise

00:24:07.112 --> 00:24:08.875
our leaders make it out to be.

00:24:08.947 --> 00:24:11.711
There are thousands of us
who feel like prisoners, and...

00:24:11.783 --> 00:24:12.977
others who...

00:24:14.920 --> 00:24:16.387
Continue.

00:24:17.489 --> 00:24:19.457
There are...

00:24:19.524 --> 00:24:22.925
rumors of a movement...

00:24:23.061 --> 00:24:25.154
people who want
to leave the ship.

00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:27.926
Some of them are willing
to take violent action.

00:24:28.033 --> 00:24:29.728
Can you be more specific?

00:24:30.802 --> 00:24:32.929
This is a trick.

00:24:33.004 --> 00:24:33.936
A trick?

00:24:34.005 --> 00:24:36.439
You're trying to get me
to expose the movement.

00:24:36.508 --> 00:24:37.805
Our leaders put you up to this.

00:24:37.876 --> 00:24:39.776
On the contrary.

00:24:39.845 --> 00:24:41.642
We haven't even
told them we found you.

00:24:41.713 --> 00:24:43.772
You're lying.

00:24:43.849 --> 00:24:45.441
I don't have time for a debate.

00:24:45.517 --> 00:24:46.916
You asked for asylum, fine.

00:24:46.985 --> 00:24:48.646
I'll consider it,

00:24:48.720 --> 00:24:50.950
but only if you
answer my questions.

00:24:51.056 --> 00:24:52.216
What movement?

00:24:55.727 --> 00:24:57.854
Contact the Varro authorities.

00:24:57.929 --> 00:25:01.126
Let them know we've found
one of their people,

00:25:01.199 --> 00:25:02.962
and take him to the brig.

00:25:06.671 --> 00:25:09.902
You can tell the authorities
that I'm not the only one.

00:25:10.008 --> 00:25:12.499
There are hundreds more like me.

00:25:26.024 --> 00:25:28.117
Learn anything about
this supposed uprising?

00:25:28.193 --> 00:25:31.526
Jippeq said the rumors
are just that... rumors...

00:25:31.596 --> 00:25:34.588
but he's questioning our
stowaway just to be certain.

00:25:34.666 --> 00:25:38.227
New protocols
for working with the Varro.

00:25:38.303 --> 00:25:40.134
After the incident
with Ensign Kim,

00:25:40.205 --> 00:25:42.571
they insisted we keep
our crews segregated.

00:25:42.641 --> 00:25:43.835
That's pretty severe.

00:25:43.909 --> 00:25:45.740
Harry violated protocol.

00:25:45.810 --> 00:25:47.175
Frankly, I understand
their position.

00:25:47.245 --> 00:25:49.941
Is that why you
came down so hard on him?

00:25:50.015 --> 00:25:53.075
A formal reprimand for being
intimate with a young woman?

00:25:53.151 --> 00:25:55.244
I know it seems
a little extreme...

00:25:55.320 --> 00:25:58.255
but I wanted to leave
a lasting impression.

00:25:58.323 --> 00:26:00.086
Chalk it up to growing pains.

00:26:00.158 --> 00:26:02.490
Well, he looks pained,
all right.

00:26:02.561 --> 00:26:04.426
Until now,
he's had a spotless record.

00:26:06.565 --> 00:26:08.396
Maybe you should reconsider.

00:26:08.466 --> 00:26:10.024
What are you implying?

00:26:10.101 --> 00:26:12.899
Are you angry
because Harry disobeyed orders

00:26:12.971 --> 00:26:14.268
or because he let you down?

00:26:14.339 --> 00:26:16.273
I set the same standards
for all my officers.

00:26:16.341 --> 00:26:18.332
If I object
to one of your decisions,

00:26:18.410 --> 00:26:21.072
you'll hear me out...
even insist I speak up.

00:26:21.146 --> 00:26:22.909
You're my First Officer.
He's an Ensign.

00:26:23.048 --> 00:26:25.243
He hasn't earned the right
to question my orders

00:26:25.317 --> 00:26:26.875
whatever his personal views.

00:26:26.952 --> 00:26:28.249
I see.

00:26:28.320 --> 00:26:30.254
Engineering to the Captain.

00:26:30.322 --> 00:26:31.254
Yes?

00:26:31.323 --> 00:26:32.756
We found something.

00:26:32.824 --> 00:26:34.382
On my way.

00:26:35.627 --> 00:26:37.254
Do your officers make a habit

00:26:37.329 --> 00:26:38.921
of seducing the species
they encounter?

00:26:39.030 --> 00:26:41.191
Certainly not,
but it's my understanding

00:26:41.266 --> 00:26:42.756
that this relationship
was consensual.

00:26:42.834 --> 00:26:44.267
I find that difficult
to believe.

00:26:44.336 --> 00:26:47.100
We don't share your cavalier
attitude toward intimacy.

00:26:47.172 --> 00:26:49.037
Our attitude is
anything but cavalier.

00:26:49.107 --> 00:26:50.734
Ensign Kim has already
been reprimanded.

00:26:50.809 --> 00:26:53.369
What about Tal?
What happens to her?

00:26:53.445 --> 00:26:55.345
In our society, mating
is taken very seriously.

00:26:55.413 --> 00:26:58.109
When two people choose each
other, the bonding is permanent.

00:26:58.183 --> 00:26:59.309
They become
biochemically linked.

00:26:59.384 --> 00:27:01.215
Separation is rare.

00:27:01.286 --> 00:27:03.311
It induces illness,
sometimes fatal.

00:27:03.388 --> 00:27:04.480
What's to become of Tal

00:27:04.556 --> 00:27:07.252
when your Ensign flies off
in search of his next conquest?

00:27:09.894 --> 00:27:11.156
Captain.

00:27:11.229 --> 00:27:12.662
You found something?

00:27:12.731 --> 00:27:14.198
We've detected microfractures

00:27:14.265 --> 00:27:15.892
in one of Voyager's
docking ports.

00:27:16.034 --> 00:27:16.898
Microfractures?

00:27:17.035 --> 00:27:18.468
That's the same problem
we've been having.

00:27:18.536 --> 00:27:19.628
A coincidence?

00:27:19.704 --> 00:27:21.501
I had suspicions that it wasn't.

00:27:21.573 --> 00:27:22.870
Seven confirmed them.

00:27:22.941 --> 00:27:24.670
Observe.
Silicon-based parasites

00:27:24.743 --> 00:27:26.335
which feed on duranium alloys.

00:27:26.411 --> 00:27:28.311
Apparently,
they began replicating

00:27:28.380 --> 00:27:30.211
on the Varro ship's hull
several months ago

00:27:30.281 --> 00:27:31.748
and then migrated to Voyager.

00:27:31.816 --> 00:27:32.748
We analyzed them

00:27:32.817 --> 00:27:35.411
and found artificial
gene sequences.

00:27:35.487 --> 00:27:37.011
The parasites are synthetic.

00:27:37.088 --> 00:27:38.919
They may have been
created by someone

00:27:39.057 --> 00:27:40.524
aboard your vessel.

00:27:40.592 --> 00:27:42.822
Sabotage?
I don't believe it.

00:27:42.894 --> 00:27:44.452
Perhaps not everyone

00:27:44.529 --> 00:27:47.362
is content to be
in your collective.

00:28:01.680 --> 00:28:02.874
Tal, are you there?

00:28:03.014 --> 00:28:04.379
Harry?

00:28:04.449 --> 00:28:05.541
I can't keep this com-link open.

00:28:05.617 --> 00:28:06.777
Where are you?

00:28:06.851 --> 00:28:08.216
By my computer.

00:28:08.286 --> 00:28:10.516
Okay.
Get ready for a ride.

00:28:10.588 --> 00:28:11.520
I'm locking on.

00:28:11.589 --> 00:28:12.613
A ride?

00:28:23.835 --> 00:28:25.166
Where are we?

00:28:25.236 --> 00:28:26.635
A shuttlecraft.

00:28:26.705 --> 00:28:27.637
Shuttlecraft?

00:28:27.706 --> 00:28:29.196
A short-range vessel.

00:28:29.274 --> 00:28:30.400
We use it for away missions.

00:28:32.110 --> 00:28:33.441
We can go anywhere we want?

00:28:33.511 --> 00:28:34.443
Anywhere.

00:28:34.512 --> 00:28:35.536
For a while anyway.

00:28:35.613 --> 00:28:38.810
I'm not due back on Voyager
until 1900 hours.

00:28:38.883 --> 00:28:41.818
They think I'm still out
repairing a hull fracture.

00:28:41.886 --> 00:28:43.444
I finished early.

00:28:46.124 --> 00:28:47.921
You're a fugitive now.

00:28:47.992 --> 00:28:50.859
How many protocols
did you break this time?

00:28:50.929 --> 00:28:52.294
Let's see...

00:28:52.363 --> 00:28:54.558
unauthorized use
of a shuttlecraft...

00:28:54.632 --> 00:28:55.792
kidnapping...

00:28:55.867 --> 00:28:58.495
Direct violation
of the Captain's orders...

00:28:59.738 --> 00:29:01.831
I must be crazy.

00:29:01.906 --> 00:29:03.271
I like you crazy.

00:29:06.010 --> 00:29:07.307
Navigation?

00:29:07.378 --> 00:29:09.403
Oh, careful.
That's the weapons array.

00:29:09.481 --> 00:29:12.041
You know, you almost vaporized
your living quarters.

00:29:13.318 --> 00:29:15.513
Well, they could use
a good cleaning.

00:29:16.855 --> 00:29:18.345
Let's go somewhere.

00:29:18.423 --> 00:29:19.788
Where?

00:29:19.858 --> 00:29:22.986
There's a nebula about
300,000 kilometers from here.

00:29:23.061 --> 00:29:25.029
I've been watching it
on the sensors

00:29:25.096 --> 00:29:26.358
for the past few days.

00:29:26.431 --> 00:29:29.366
Oh, I would love to see it
with my own eyes.

00:29:29.434 --> 00:29:30.560
Have a seat.

00:29:42.380 --> 00:29:44.610
Look at this...
a subspace vacuole

00:29:44.682 --> 00:29:46.206
near the center of the cloud.

00:29:46.284 --> 00:29:49.720
It must act
as a gravitational anchor.

00:29:49.788 --> 00:29:54.350
There's so much data here,
it'll take weeks to analyze.

00:29:54.425 --> 00:29:56.450
Do you have a storage device?

00:29:56.528 --> 00:29:58.325
We need to download
these readings.

00:29:58.396 --> 00:29:59.420
What?

00:29:59.497 --> 00:30:00.930
I've just never seen

00:30:00.999 --> 00:30:03.934
anyone so excited about
a class-3 nebula before.

00:30:04.068 --> 00:30:06.628
Maybe you've been taking them
for granted.

00:30:06.704 --> 00:30:08.604
Maybe I have.

00:30:10.175 --> 00:30:11.836
Don't stop.

00:30:14.245 --> 00:30:16.805
You're beautiful
when you're scanning.

00:30:16.881 --> 00:30:19.406
Is that what you say to every
girl you take for a ride?

00:30:19.484 --> 00:30:20.951
I bet you've left a trail

00:30:21.085 --> 00:30:23.952
of broken hearts
across the Delta Quadrant.

00:30:24.088 --> 00:30:25.248
Actually...

00:30:29.127 --> 00:30:30.651
Problem?

00:30:30.728 --> 00:30:33.390
Stray radiation from the nebula.

00:30:33.464 --> 00:30:35.455
I thought it was
the proximity alarm.

00:30:35.533 --> 00:30:37.967
You said we had
a couple of hours.

00:30:38.036 --> 00:30:41.267
No one's going
to come looking for us.

00:30:41.339 --> 00:30:42.829
Oh, you don't know
Commander Tuvok.

00:30:42.907 --> 00:30:44.841
If he sees one electron
out of place,

00:30:44.909 --> 00:30:46.376
he calls for Red Alert.

00:30:50.448 --> 00:30:52.143
Here we are alone,

00:30:52.217 --> 00:30:56.153
and all I can think about
is duty and orders.

00:30:56.221 --> 00:30:58.348
Those things are important.

00:30:58.423 --> 00:31:00.948
I think about them, too.

00:31:01.025 --> 00:31:05.724
But sometimes you need to follow
a different kind of protocol.

00:31:05.797 --> 00:31:08.459
If you believe in something
strongly enough,

00:31:08.533 --> 00:31:10.057
you can't ignore it...

00:31:10.134 --> 00:31:13.467
even if it means
breaking a few rules.

00:31:13.538 --> 00:31:17.201
That's why I took this shuttle,
but every time I break a rule,

00:31:17.275 --> 00:31:21.143
I feel like my skull
is going to decompress.

00:31:21.212 --> 00:31:24.045
I'm like some kind
of... Borg drone...

00:31:24.115 --> 00:31:25.605
programmed...

00:31:25.683 --> 00:31:28.948
except I was designed to be
the perfect Starfleet officer.

00:31:29.087 --> 00:31:30.554
Top of his class...

00:31:30.622 --> 00:31:33.682
captain of the velocity
team, interstellar honors.

00:31:33.758 --> 00:31:35.282
First field assignment...

00:31:35.360 --> 00:31:37.658
Bridge officer on a starship.

00:31:37.729 --> 00:31:39.219
Every cadet's dream come true.

00:31:41.399 --> 00:31:43.890
You're not a program.

00:31:43.968 --> 00:31:47.096
In fact, I envy your freedom.

00:31:47.171 --> 00:31:49.901
I mean, your crew's mission...
to seek out life...

00:31:49.974 --> 00:31:52.374
what could be more liberating?

00:31:52.443 --> 00:31:54.536
You explore the unknown.

00:31:56.381 --> 00:32:00.442
Don't be afraid to explore
what's happening between us.

00:32:07.992 --> 00:32:09.186
Oh, no.

00:32:09.260 --> 00:32:11.023
The Delta Flyer.

00:32:11.095 --> 00:32:12.255
Commander Tuvok?

00:32:12.330 --> 00:32:13.922
We're being hailed.

00:32:18.169 --> 00:32:22.230
Well, you better answer them
before they open fire.

00:32:25.009 --> 00:32:26.408
Kim here.

00:32:26.477 --> 00:32:27.774
Ensign, you are

00:32:27.845 --> 00:32:29.938
in direct violation
of the Captain's orders.

00:32:30.014 --> 00:32:33.916
Return to Voyager immediately
and bring Derran Tal with you.

00:32:33.985 --> 00:32:36.112
Yes, sir, but why bring Tal?

00:32:36.187 --> 00:32:38.348
She's wanted
by the Varro authorities

00:32:38.423 --> 00:32:40.914
regarding an act of sabotage.

00:32:48.199 --> 00:32:50.326
There's no point in lying.

00:32:50.401 --> 00:32:51.800
We found a schematic
for the parasite

00:32:51.869 --> 00:32:53.803
on your personal database.

00:32:53.871 --> 00:32:57.432
You realize this could
destroy our ship, our home?

00:32:57.508 --> 00:32:59.567
To some of us,
it's more like a prison.

00:32:59.644 --> 00:33:02.078
So you've resorted to sabotage,

00:33:02.146 --> 00:33:03.613
no doubt involving him.

00:33:03.681 --> 00:33:05.649
Mr. Kim's complicity
remains to be proven.

00:33:05.717 --> 00:33:08.083
He had nothing to do
with our movement.

00:33:08.152 --> 00:33:09.141
"Movement"?

00:33:09.220 --> 00:33:10.152
Tell them.

00:33:10.221 --> 00:33:12.246
It's none of their concern.

00:33:12.323 --> 00:33:13.847
If you want our help,
you'll need to explain.

00:33:13.925 --> 00:33:15.859
She's referring to a small group
of dissidents...

00:33:15.927 --> 00:33:16.894
It's not a small group.

00:33:16.961 --> 00:33:17.893
There are hundreds of us.

00:33:17.962 --> 00:33:19.259
What are you trying to achieve?

00:33:19.330 --> 00:33:20.456
Our freedom...

00:33:20.531 --> 00:33:22.522
the right to live as we choose,

00:33:22.600 --> 00:33:23.726
to go where we choose.

00:33:23.801 --> 00:33:25.928
How will you accomplish that
if your vessel is destroyed?

00:33:26.037 --> 00:33:27.937
We're not trying to destroy it.

00:33:28.039 --> 00:33:29.734
We're trying to dismantle it.

00:33:29.807 --> 00:33:31.934
The parasites
weren't placed randomly.

00:33:32.043 --> 00:33:34.944
They're targeting the linkages
between segments.

00:33:35.013 --> 00:33:37.345
Each segment will
become its own ship.

00:33:37.415 --> 00:33:40.816
People can decide
whether to go or stay.

00:33:40.885 --> 00:33:42.216
You're destroying the work

00:33:42.286 --> 00:33:44.948
of every generation
that came before you.

00:33:45.023 --> 00:33:47.958
Our ship isn't
just a collection of modules.

00:33:48.026 --> 00:33:50.551
It's an expression
of unity, tradition.

00:33:50.628 --> 00:33:53.461
For the sake of our history,
we must respect the rights of...

00:33:53.531 --> 00:33:54.463
Of the majority.

00:33:54.532 --> 00:33:55.464
Yes.

00:33:55.533 --> 00:33:56.795
What about the rights
of the minority?

00:33:56.868 --> 00:34:00.599
Tal... if those segments
come apart,

00:34:00.671 --> 00:34:02.764
there could be
decompressive explosions...

00:34:02.840 --> 00:34:04.501
most likely casualties.

00:34:04.575 --> 00:34:06.167
Is that what you want?

00:34:06.244 --> 00:34:09.179
You know more
about the parasites than we do.

00:34:09.247 --> 00:34:10.578
You could help us.

00:34:10.648 --> 00:34:11.910
Captain, she's a criminal.

00:34:12.050 --> 00:34:14.746
And maybe your only chance
of stopping a catastrophe.

00:34:14.819 --> 00:34:17.287
Set up a datalink with Voyager.

00:34:17.355 --> 00:34:19.414
We'll do what we can
from our end.

00:34:19.490 --> 00:34:21.151
Tal...

00:34:23.594 --> 00:34:25.459
I'll help you
slow down the parasites,

00:34:25.530 --> 00:34:27.828
so you can evacuate
the segments in danger...

00:34:27.899 --> 00:34:29.560
nothing more.

00:34:29.634 --> 00:34:31.124
Let's get started.

00:34:37.041 --> 00:34:37.939
Captain...

00:34:38.042 --> 00:34:39.066
Stow it, Ensign.

00:34:39.143 --> 00:34:40.770
Right now,
the only thing standing

00:34:40.845 --> 00:34:42.813
between you and the brig
is this report.

00:34:42.880 --> 00:34:44.279
The Doctor's bio-scans

00:34:44.348 --> 00:34:46.179
confirm that you and Tal
have developed

00:34:46.250 --> 00:34:47.649
some sort
of biochemical bond.

00:34:47.718 --> 00:34:49.447
Clearly, it's affected
your behavior,

00:34:49.520 --> 00:34:52.250
so I have to assume that's
why you disobeyed my orders.

00:34:52.323 --> 00:34:53.517
Report to Sick Bay.

00:34:53.591 --> 00:34:55.616
You'll be confined there
until this is over.

00:34:58.329 --> 00:34:59.296
Captain!

00:34:59.363 --> 00:35:00.955
I told you to report
for treatment!

00:35:01.099 --> 00:35:03.260
I don't want treatment!

00:35:03.334 --> 00:35:05.131
In my ready room.

00:35:09.507 --> 00:35:10.701
You've got 30 seconds

00:35:10.775 --> 00:35:12.743
before I have Tuvok drag you
to Sick Bay.

00:35:12.810 --> 00:35:13.902
Captain, I am not sick.

00:35:13.978 --> 00:35:15.377
I didn't disobey your orders

00:35:15.446 --> 00:35:17.414
because I'm under
some alien influence.

00:35:17.482 --> 00:35:20.110
I disobeyed your orders
because Tal and I are in love,

00:35:20.184 --> 00:35:22.118
and it's not right
for you to keep us apart.

00:35:22.186 --> 00:35:23.619
Listen to yourself.

00:35:23.688 --> 00:35:25.918
You don't sound anything
like the Harry Kim I know.

00:35:26.023 --> 00:35:28.355
Good. I have served
on this ship for five years

00:35:28.426 --> 00:35:29.415
and said, "yes, ma'am"

00:35:29.494 --> 00:35:31.052
to every one of your orders,
but not this time.

00:35:31.129 --> 00:35:32.619
You're willing
to risk your rank,

00:35:32.697 --> 00:35:34.995
your career over this?

00:35:37.001 --> 00:35:39.401
Have you ever been in love,
Captain?

00:35:39.470 --> 00:35:41.165
Your point?

00:35:41.239 --> 00:35:43.264
Did your skin ever flush

00:35:43.341 --> 00:35:45.275
when you were near
another person?

00:35:45.343 --> 00:35:47.937
Did your stomach
ever feel like someone

00:35:48.012 --> 00:35:49.138
hollowed it out with a knife

00:35:49.213 --> 00:35:50.942
when you were apart?

00:35:51.015 --> 00:35:54.280
Did your throat ever swell
when you realized it was over?

00:35:54.352 --> 00:35:56.081
Seven of Nine...

00:35:56.154 --> 00:35:58.884
Seven of Nine told me
love's like a disease.

00:35:58.956 --> 00:36:01.516
Well, maybe it is...
pheromones, endorphins,

00:36:01.592 --> 00:36:05.050
chemicals in our blood
changing our responses,

00:36:05.129 --> 00:36:07.256
physical discomfort,

00:36:07.331 --> 00:36:09.196
but any way you look
at it, it's still love.

00:36:09.267 --> 00:36:11.895
For the sake of argument,
let's say you're right.

00:36:11.969 --> 00:36:13.903
Your feelings for Tal
are no different

00:36:14.005 --> 00:36:15.404
than mine for... what?

00:36:15.473 --> 00:36:17.304
The man I was engaged to marry?

00:36:17.375 --> 00:36:20.469
Well, I lost him,
and you're going to lose Tal.

00:36:20.545 --> 00:36:21.637
You know that.

00:36:21.712 --> 00:36:25.113
What the Doctor is offering you
is a way to ease the pain.

00:36:27.218 --> 00:36:29.186
That man you were
going to marry...

00:36:29.253 --> 00:36:32.552
if you could have
just taken a hypospray

00:36:32.623 --> 00:36:34.284
to make yourself stop loving him

00:36:34.358 --> 00:36:38.124
so that it didn't hurt so much
when you were away from him,

00:36:38.196 --> 00:36:40.994
would you have done that?

00:36:42.366 --> 00:36:43.731
Captain to the Bridge.

00:36:47.205 --> 00:36:50.766
We're detecting structural
breaches on the Varro ship.

00:36:50.841 --> 00:36:52.866
Take your station.

00:36:52.944 --> 00:36:56.038
Their shields are weakening.

00:36:56.113 --> 00:36:58.638
One of the junctions
is about to decompress.

00:36:58.716 --> 00:36:59.842
On screen.

00:37:03.254 --> 00:37:04.516
Mr. Paris, release
the docking clamps.

00:37:04.589 --> 00:37:06.523
Back us away.

00:37:06.591 --> 00:37:08.183
Docking controls are off-line.

00:37:08.259 --> 00:37:09.817
I can't break us free.

00:37:25.776 --> 00:37:27.607
Their shields
are continuing to weaken.

00:37:27.678 --> 00:37:29.043
The superstructure
will collapse

00:37:29.113 --> 00:37:30.637
in less than three minutes.

00:37:30.715 --> 00:37:32.410
If that happens while
we're still docked...

00:37:32.483 --> 00:37:34.007
Keep trying to break free.

00:37:34.085 --> 00:37:36.053
Janeway to Varro control room.

00:37:36.120 --> 00:37:37.052
What's your status?

00:37:37.121 --> 00:37:38.884
Tal was able
to slow the parasites' growth

00:37:38.956 --> 00:37:40.116
with a polaron surge,

00:37:40.191 --> 00:37:42.091
but the junctions
are still destabilizing.

00:37:42.159 --> 00:37:45.026
How much longer until you've
evacuated the affected areas?

00:37:46.063 --> 00:37:47.894
We need another two minutes
at least.

00:37:47.965 --> 00:37:50.798
I've got the docking controls
back on line.

00:37:50.868 --> 00:37:52.335
Initiate decompression sequence.

00:37:52.403 --> 00:37:54.303
Wait. If we stay where we are,

00:37:54.372 --> 00:37:56.602
and extend Voyager's
structural integrity field

00:37:56.674 --> 00:37:57.732
around the Varro ship,

00:37:57.808 --> 00:37:59.207
we could buy them
another minute or two.

00:37:59.277 --> 00:38:00.869
They could finish
the evacuation.

00:38:00.945 --> 00:38:02.537
However,
if an explosion occurs

00:38:02.613 --> 00:38:04.240
while both ships
are inside the field,

00:38:04.315 --> 00:38:06.146
neither vessel will survive.

00:38:06.217 --> 00:38:07.844
We can do it, Captain.

00:38:09.387 --> 00:38:10.752
Keep us where we are.

00:38:10.821 --> 00:38:12.345
Janeway to Engineering.

00:38:12.423 --> 00:38:13.856
Torres here.

00:38:13.924 --> 00:38:16.449
Divert all available power
to the integrity field

00:38:16.527 --> 00:38:18.893
and extend it around
the Varro ship.

00:38:19.030 --> 00:38:20.224
Understood.

00:38:22.033 --> 00:38:24.467
Voyager is reinforcing
our shields.

00:38:24.535 --> 00:38:25.866
Surprising, isn't it?

00:38:25.936 --> 00:38:29.064
A ship of outsiders risking
their lives to save ours.

00:38:29.140 --> 00:38:30.698
They're unusual people.

00:38:30.775 --> 00:38:33.835
Or maybe the galaxy
isn't as hostile as you think.

00:38:33.911 --> 00:38:36.402
All junctions are clear.

00:38:38.482 --> 00:38:40.006
What are you waiting for?

00:38:40.084 --> 00:38:41.676
Tell Voyager to move away.

00:38:41.752 --> 00:38:43.913
I'm initiating
another polaron surge.

00:38:44.055 --> 00:38:45.920
We can destroy these parasites.

00:38:45.990 --> 00:38:47.252
It's too late.

00:38:47.325 --> 00:38:49.623
You'll only destroy Voyager
along with our ship.

00:38:53.097 --> 00:38:54.928
Let them go.

00:38:55.066 --> 00:38:56.863
Let us go.

00:39:02.173 --> 00:39:03.470
Tal to Voyager.

00:39:03.541 --> 00:39:05.270
The evacuation's complete.

00:39:05.343 --> 00:39:09.439
Disengage your structural field
and move to a safe distance.

00:39:09.513 --> 00:39:11.811
Releasing docking clamps.

00:39:41.579 --> 00:39:43.274
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:39:43.347 --> 00:39:46.111
Most of the Varro
have opted to stay together

00:39:46.183 --> 00:39:49.380
traveling in separate ships,
but the dissident group

00:39:49.453 --> 00:39:51.921
has been granted permission
to break away

00:39:52.056 --> 00:39:53.318
and find their own path.

00:39:53.391 --> 00:39:54.483
We wish them luck.

00:39:55.726 --> 00:39:56.954
Come in.

00:40:02.600 --> 00:40:04.727
I wasn't sure I'd see you again.

00:40:04.802 --> 00:40:07.168
The Captain gave me permission
to say good-bye.

00:40:07.238 --> 00:40:10.366
How are you feeling?

00:40:10.441 --> 00:40:12.534
Lovesick.

00:40:12.610 --> 00:40:14.601
Me, too.

00:40:14.678 --> 00:40:16.168
Will you manage?

00:40:18.215 --> 00:40:19.910
We have medications.

00:40:19.984 --> 00:40:22.544
I'll recover eventually.

00:40:25.990 --> 00:40:27.617
So, where are you going?

00:40:31.762 --> 00:40:33.855
The Natori system.

00:40:33.931 --> 00:40:38.061
A pair of binary stars
caught in each other's gravity.

00:40:38.135 --> 00:40:40.968
We passed within a parsec
three months ago,

00:40:41.105 --> 00:40:43.471
and now we're going
back for a real look.

00:40:43.541 --> 00:40:45.372
Do me one favor.

00:40:47.645 --> 00:40:49.135
Anything.

00:40:50.548 --> 00:40:54.575
Next time you run across
a class-3 nebula,

00:40:54.652 --> 00:40:56.381
think of me.

00:40:58.956 --> 00:41:02.585
Chronic sleep loss,
acute gastroenteritis...

00:41:02.660 --> 00:41:04.218
you must feel awful,

00:41:04.295 --> 00:41:07.093
yet you're still
refusing treatment?

00:41:07.164 --> 00:41:09.655
Captain, just the person
I wanted to see.

00:41:09.733 --> 00:41:11.462
This nonsense has
gone on long enough.

00:41:11.535 --> 00:41:13.025
Order Mr. Kim
to take his medicine.

00:41:13.103 --> 00:41:14.468
Is his condition fatal?

00:41:14.538 --> 00:41:15.937
That's hardly the point.

00:41:16.040 --> 00:41:18.133
Will he recover
without taking his medicine?

00:41:18.209 --> 00:41:20.575
Yes, but it could take weeks,
even months.

00:41:20.644 --> 00:41:24.136
Well, then, if Mr. Kim
wants to suffer...

00:41:25.616 --> 00:41:26.878
Sometimes I think
everyone on this ship

00:41:26.951 --> 00:41:29.112
has been possessed
by alien hormones.

00:41:29.186 --> 00:41:30.710
Would you excuse us, please?

00:41:33.691 --> 00:41:34.623
Thank you.

00:41:34.692 --> 00:41:35.716
Oh, don't thank me.

00:41:35.793 --> 00:41:38.091
I have no intention
of relieving you of your duties,

00:41:38.162 --> 00:41:39.288
no matter how lousy you feel.

00:41:39.363 --> 00:41:40.421
I understand.

00:41:40.498 --> 00:41:42.489
And the reprimand still stands.

00:41:46.003 --> 00:41:48.471
I've been thinking
about how I reacted

00:41:48.539 --> 00:41:50.564
to your relationship with Tal.

00:41:50.641 --> 00:41:54.839
You reacted
like any Captain would.

00:41:54.912 --> 00:41:57.972
Probably, but I
can't help wondering

00:41:58.048 --> 00:42:01.415
if my response would
have been the same

00:42:01.485 --> 00:42:05.387
if it had been, say,
Tom Paris instead of you.

00:42:05.456 --> 00:42:07.117
Oh, don't get me wrong.

00:42:07.191 --> 00:42:11.924
I still would have been
angry and disappointed, but...

00:42:11.996 --> 00:42:14.556
I wouldn't have been surprised.

00:42:14.632 --> 00:42:18.295
Because Ensign Kim
doesn't break the rules.

00:42:20.704 --> 00:42:24.071
The truth is, Harry...

00:42:24.141 --> 00:42:27.542
I think about you differently
than the rest of the crew.

00:42:27.611 --> 00:42:30.136
Which isn't to suggest
that I don't care

00:42:30.214 --> 00:42:32.273
deeply about each of them,
but...

00:42:32.349 --> 00:42:34.943
you came to me fresh
out of the Academy,

00:42:35.019 --> 00:42:36.714
wide-eyed with excitement

00:42:36.787 --> 00:42:39.381
about your first
deep space assignment.

00:42:39.456 --> 00:42:41.924
From that first day,
I've always felt

00:42:41.992 --> 00:42:44.654
more protective of you
than the others.

00:42:47.264 --> 00:42:49.459
I appreciate that...

00:42:49.533 --> 00:42:52.627
but that was five years ago.

00:42:54.638 --> 00:42:56.970
I've changed.

00:42:57.107 --> 00:42:59.098
Yes, you have.

00:43:00.511 --> 00:43:03.674
Maybe I'm not
the perfect officer anymore.

00:43:03.747 --> 00:43:06.045
Maybe not...

00:43:08.852 --> 00:43:11.320
but you're a better man.

00:43:25.035 --> 00:43:27.003
Last call.

00:43:28.138 --> 00:43:29.867
There's a bowl of soup
in storage,

00:43:29.940 --> 00:43:31.737
and I left
the replicator on line.

00:43:31.809 --> 00:43:33.401
Thanks.

00:43:33.477 --> 00:43:35.377
Good night.

00:43:41.819 --> 00:43:43.582
Oh, I was just closing
up for the evening,

00:43:43.654 --> 00:43:44.780
but if you need anything...

00:43:44.855 --> 00:43:46.117
I'm here to see Ensign Kim.

00:43:46.190 --> 00:43:48.658
Oh. Good luck.

00:43:53.631 --> 00:43:54.757
Ensign.

00:43:54.832 --> 00:43:55.992
Hmm?

00:43:57.234 --> 00:43:59.225
Thank you.

00:43:59.303 --> 00:44:00.634
For what?

00:44:00.704 --> 00:44:01.864
You completed several

00:44:01.939 --> 00:44:03.998
of my astrometric scans
this morning.

00:44:04.074 --> 00:44:05.473
You're welcome.

00:44:05.542 --> 00:44:08.340
I had some time
between duty shifts.

00:44:08.412 --> 00:44:10.778
Besides, it kept me occupied.

00:44:10.848 --> 00:44:13.316
You are attempting
to distract yourself

00:44:13.384 --> 00:44:15.147
from your emotional damage.

00:44:15.219 --> 00:44:17.483
I wish I could say
it was working.

00:44:17.554 --> 00:44:20.421
A treatment to relieve
your condition was available

00:44:20.491 --> 00:44:22.356
and yet you refused.

00:44:22.426 --> 00:44:24.223
I've got a disease,

00:44:24.294 --> 00:44:26.922
but I'm willing
to live with the symptoms.

00:44:27.031 --> 00:44:28.623
Doesn't make much sense does it?

00:44:32.236 --> 00:44:35.797
I assumed that romantic love
was a human weakness,

00:44:35.873 --> 00:44:39.240
but clearly it can also be
a source of strength.

00:44:40.611 --> 00:44:43.205
Perhaps my analogy was flawed.

00:44:43.280 --> 00:44:45.248
Love is not a disease.

00:44:48.285 --> 00:44:50.446
Get well soon.
